# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the root .dockerignore, so this keeps
# the SageMaker build context tight without changing what the other root-context builds in this
# repo (scripts/docker, examples/*) see.
#
# Exclude everything, then re-include only the paths sagemaker/Dockerfile actually copies.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!README.md
!LICENSE
!packages/
!src/
!scripts/
!assets/
!sagemaker/

# Re-exclude junk living inside the re-included directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
